From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:23:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32: Keep the classic event logs, in files shared by
 every process.

ReportEvent wrote nothing (Word reports one event as it starts), and
ReadEventLog, the counts, backups and clearing were stubs.  Each log is
now a file in the classic format in system32\winevt\Logs, a named mutex
around every access to it and a named event pulsed for
NotifyChangeEventLog.  A source writes to the log of that name, to the
log whose key names it, or to Application.  Records have the layout
Windows 11 gives them -- the user SID at the next 8-byte boundary after
the computer name, strings and data right after, the whole padded to
8 bytes with its length last -- and reads move as on Windows: a
sequential read goes on from the last record the previous read gave,
in either direction, a seek read starts at the record asked for, and a
read gives as many whole records as fit (tools/startupgapsprobe
evtread).  Numbering goes on after a log is cleared; a log about to
outgrow its MaxSize drops its oldest records.  The event log service
writes the version (6009) and that it started (6005) to the System log
when it starts, and that it stopped (6006), as Windows does.  The
upstream tests pass without their todos; the reads that seek to the
tenth record of the System log are skipped while it has fewer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/advapi32/Makefile.in b/dlls/advapi32/Makefile.in
index a2ec5adba8b..8b0bc7acb47 100644
--- a/dlls/advapi32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/Makefile.in
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	advapi32.rc \
 	cred.c \
 	crypt.c \
+	classiclog.c \
 	eventlog.c \
 	lsa.c \
 	registry.c \
diff --git a/dlls/advapi32/classiclog.c b/dlls/advapi32/classiclog.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..f6b35f3aced
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/classiclog.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1262 @@
+/*
+ * The classic event logs: OpenEventLog, RegisterEventSource, ReportEvent, ReadEventLog and the rest
+ *
+ * Copyright 2026 the Wine Altars project
